>
> I've read that the best way to polypile is to make multiple stacks of
> each item class, and then zap the \oPoly along the line.  How many
> items can I put in each stack before I run a risk golemization?  What's
> the chance that I'll get xDSM by polying a stack of normal armor?  Are
> unihorns guaranteed to poly into magic markers?  What other tools will
> change into useful stuff when polyed?  I have masses of tin whistles,
> mirrors and other useless stuff.

No, you are not guaranteed to get anything.  You have a certain chance.
 Your choice of original items in piles change the odds of getting
useful things.

The specific number crunching aside, there are two kinds of items.
Magic and non-magic.  It's highly unlikely for non-magic items to
become magic, and *magic* marker is indeed magic tool.  So if you ever
want a magic marker via polypiling, it's very very very unlikely that
you get one polypiling non-magic tools.  That's why people use unihorns
(the most accessible magic tools) to get magic markers.  However, it's
never guaranteed.

So you want to poly 'magic' tools if you want something useful.  I
don't know the list of magic tools off the top of my head, but I think
things like figurines and such are magic tools (many of them are not
very exciting).  I like almost all of other tools, so I'm hesitant to
poly them.  I suppose magical horns are disposable for wizards...


